<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=5.0, minimum-scale=1.0">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="ie=edge">
    <meta name="Description" content="How dwaynecodling.com measures visits and handles messages">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Privacy | Dwayne Codling" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="How dwaynecodling.com measures visits and handles messages" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://dwaynecodling.com/privacy" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://dwaynecodling.com/privacy" />
    <title>Privacy | Dwayne Codling</title>
    <%- include("../partials/links") %>
    <style>
        .privacy-page {
            max-width: 72rem;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 8rem 2rem;
        }

        .privacy-page h1 {
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
            font-size: var(--heading-2);
            font-weight: 700;
            color: #f4ede0;
            margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
        }

        .privacy-page h2 {
            font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
            font-size: 2.4rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: #f4ede0;
            margin: 4rem 0 1.2rem;
        }

        .privacy-page p,
        .privacy-page li {
            font-size: 1.7rem;
            line-height: 3rem;
            color: #a89e90;
        }

        .privacy-page p {
            margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
        }

        .privacy-page ul {
            padding-left: 2rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
        }

        .privacy-page__consent {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 1.6rem;
        }

        .privacy-page a {
            color: #c8853a;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<%- include("../partials/nav") %>

<main class="content" role="main">
    <div class="container">
        <article class="privacy-page">
            <h1>Privacy</h1>
            <p>Last updated 14 November 2026.</p>

            <h2>Visits</h2>
            <p>I use Cloudflare Web Analytics to see how many people visit and which pages they read. It sets no cookies and doesn't track you across sites. I see totals only, such as:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>pages viewed</li>
                <li>the site that sent you here</li>
                <li>country, device type and browser</li>
                <li>how quickly pages load</li>
            </ul>
            <p>This doesn't identify you. If you'd rather not be counted, a content blocker will stop it.</p>

            <h2>Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity (optional)</h2>
            <p>If you click Accept on the cookie banner, two more tools run, both loaded through Google Tag Manager:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> sets cookies to recognise return visits and records the pages you view and actions such as sending the contact form. Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a> applies.</li>
                <li><strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> records how pages are used (scrolling, clicks and mouse movement) so I can see where the site is hard to use. Anything you type into a form is hidden from the recordings. Microsoft's <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy statement</a> applies.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If you click Reject, or choose nothing, neither tool runs or sets cookies. You can change your choice at any time:</p>
            <p class="privacy-page__consent"><button type="button" class="hero__button hero__button--outline" data-consent-open>Cookie settings</button> <span data-consent-status></span></p>

            <h2>Messages</h2>
            <p>If you use the <a href="/contact-me">contact form</a>, your name, email address and message are emailed to me (sent through Resend) so I can reply. I don't add you to any list.</p>
            <p>The form uses Google reCAPTCHA to block spam. Google's <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a> applies to that check.</p>

            <h2>Embedded content</h2>
            <p>Some posts include YouTube videos (in privacy-enhanced mode) or Instagram posts. These load from those services, and their own privacy policies apply.</p>

            <h2>Questions</h2>
            <p>If you'd like me to delete a message you sent, or have a question, get in touch through the <a href="/contact-me">contact page</a>.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</main>

<%- include("../partials/footer") %>
</body>
</html>
